{"Queue shutdown uses Python 3.13-only APIs (queue.ShutDown and q.shutdown) without compatibility guards, causing AttributeError/NameError on older supported Python versions": 0.8800671100616455, "Uptime CLI help still only documents the legacy parallel modes (serial, parallel, batched-parallel) and does not include thread-queue-parallel, preventing users from discovering or selecting the new queue mode": 0.029092803597450256, "OffsetTracker can advance commits past completed messages after a gap because get_committable_offsets() never removes offsets from outstanding when committed, and mark_committed() trims all_offsets allowing later calls to over-advance and commit unprocessed offsets": 0.2751213610172272, "Thread-queue mode selection has conflicting behavior - constructor may reject thread-queue-parallel or accept it but create_with_partitions() falls back to serial, needs verification against actual factory implementation": 0.03850075602531433, "Thread-queue mode commits the last processed offset instead of the next offset to read, mixing two different conventions between OffsetTracker and commit wrapper which can cause data loss after restart": 0.20410515367984772, "Offset-commit tests only assert final committed offset after all messages drain, not validating exact next-offset-to-read contract at commit time, which would not catch regressions where queue worker commits too early or uses wrong offset convention": 0.3008365333080292}